Replace-From: David Yang <mmyangfl@gmail.com>
Replace-Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 03:29:48 +0800
Subject: net: phy: add support for HiSilicon Festa PHYs


HiSilicon STB SoCs integrate a Festa gigabit Ethernet PHY whose
behaviour is defined by microcode; boards whose bootloader does not load
the image from an external EEPROM need someone to inject it over MDIO.

The device only accepts microcode while powered down, and its expanded
MDIO window lets the entry point be written last so the core can never
fetch a half loaded instruction.

Add a driver matching the known Festa IDs which downloads
hisilicon/festa.<phy_id>.ucode on every PHY init sequence. A board
without an installed image keeps running whatever the PHY was started
with, so a missing firmware file is not an error; a failed download is.

Signed-off-by: David Yang <mmyangfl@gmail.com>
 3 files changed, 205 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 drivers/net/phy/hisi-festa.c


